From 43df9468febc173e6cf9363d87e8ad34e76d7434 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Dodds <mike@oath.tech>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:11:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Support register BT with modulo offsets and undefined flags

Register operands only; unsupported memory and immediate forms fail closed. CF receives the indexed bit, with modulo operand width; all other status flags, including vendor-dependent ZF, are undefined. Focused Lean checks exercise both ZF values for either incoming value at every supported width. The native comparison reads CF only. Supply the test runner Bool generator required by earlier consumer ISA extensions.
---
